  "gameDescriptionHtml": "\n<p>You come home from a long day at work, go to bed, and when you wake up, something’s very different…</p>\n<p>The game revolves entirely around Liminal Spaces, but what exactly are they? Liminality refers to something stuck between two different places or states. Liminal Spaces embody this, serving as areas in a state of transition. But when you stumble upon these places devoid of life, it’s eerie. You’d expect company, but it’s just you… or at least you believe so.</p>\n<p>The poolrooms are a series of big, dimly lit spaces filled with lukewarm water. These eerie, empty areas seem to stretch on forever, mixing a weird sense of calm with creeping dread. As you wander through the quiet water and deserted halls, the unsettling silence makes you wonder if you’re really alone.</p>\n",
